@startuml owner-apply-order
!include _theme.iuml

participant "Applier" as Applier
participant "Organisation settings" as Settings
participant "Property definitions" as Definitions
participant "Teams" as Teams
participant "Team membership" as Membership
participant "Organisation roles" as Roles
participant "Organisation rulesets" as Rulesets
participant "Repositories" as Repos

Applier -> Settings : one PATCH for every declared field
note right
  Sent first so a lowered base permission is
  never briefly wider than the file asks for.
end note

Applier -> Definitions : one write per property
note right
  The current definition is read before it is
  written, because the endpoint replaces.
end note

group Ordered by the dependency graph
  Applier -> Teams : create, update or delete
  Teams --> Applier : outcome per team
  Applier -> Membership : add, promote or remove
  note right
    A member of a team created in this same run
    waits for that team. If it failed, this is
    blocked rather than attempted.
  end note
  Applier -> Roles : grant or revoke
  note right
    A team granted a role waits for the team
    for the same reason.
  end note
end

Applier -> Rulesets : create or update
note right
  Last of the owner-level work: it reaches
  repositories the file may never name.
end note

Applier -> Repos : per-repository plan
note right
  Every repository is worked on only after the
  account above it agrees with the file.
end note
@enduml
